/-!
# Traps for 25 blocks of period 10, from one background of period ten whose edge driven right halves enter

A right half driven by $0000010001$ locks column 1 inside a trap of 16 cells with 100 states, the closure of its true
window under both values of the cell beyond (`ten0`). Carried leftward by its chain, as in [NineTraps](NineTraps.md),
it gives a trap of $16 + d$ cells and 100 states for the block at each distance $d$: the chain repeats with period 155
in the distance, and every block of period 10 in it appears by distance 30. Here the kernel checks the traps of the 25
blocks of the chain that the kit does not exclude.

* `tenTraps`, `tenTraps_check`: the traps, all passing the check of [WordTraps](WordTraps.md).
* `tenTraps_blocks`: their blocks.
* `ten_absorption_excludes`: for each of them, if every finitely supported right half driven by the block enters its
  trap, the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-ten`. The natural-language argument is `TenTraps.md`,
beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

